// The typed tree: what sema produces and `lower` consumes. One node per expression, statement and pattern,
// each an `Id` in a sema `Pool` with a resolved `Ty`, and calls already bound to their target (fn,
// method, `#[impl]` fn, generic instance, `dyn` slot, built-in op). Spans on the side (`base/ids` `Spans`).
//
// Part of module j3c.sema.
// Port of: (new in plan 11 B11.1; the typing half of `check/lower/*`, whose files are on `lower/*` lines)
// J3: Nothing in here needs the AST again: `lower`, the frame-string check and the LSP read only this.
// Every `match` over its node kinds is exhaustive (plan 11 B7).
module j3c.sema;
